---
description: Espresso dial-in app project rules
alwaysApply: true
---

# Stack (fixed — do not substitute; ask before adding any other dependency)

- Vite + React 18 + TypeScript (strict)
- Tailwind CSS
- Dexie.js (IndexedDB) for persistence. No backend, no auth, no cloud sync.
- React Router
- Vitest
- vite-plugin-pwa (installable, offline; used on a phone next to the machine)

# Rules

- Units: grams, seconds, °C, bar, ppm as CaCO3.
- Pure domain logic lives in `src/domain/`, has no React imports, and every function has a Vitest test.
- Derived values (ratio, daysOffRoast, extractionYieldPct) are computed, never stored.
- Mobile-first, ≥44px touch targets, one-handed use.
- Numeric inputs use `inputMode="decimal"`, accept a comma as the decimal separator, and show grams to 0.1 g.
- No analytics and no external network calls.
